# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED ARTIFACTS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Committing generated files is normally bad practice, and the large
# intermediates below stay ignored for exactly that reason. The SMALL set the
# dashboard actually reads is committed deliberately: Streamlit Community Cloud
# has no build step that could run the offline pipeline, and the architecture
# requires the app to read pre-generated artifacts rather than train anything.
# Without them a deployment would start with nothing to serve.
#
# Safe to commit because they are deterministic (verified byte-identical across
# independent runs) and every one carries the raw-CSV and master-series SHA-256,
# so a stale copy is detectable rather than silently served. A test asserts the
# committed artifacts match the current data hash.

*.parquet
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
data/processed/

# Interim data: everything except the two files the deployed app reads.
data/interim/*
!data/interim/.gitkeep
!data/interim/master_series.parquet
!data/interim/provenance.json

# Forecast artifacts: dashboard-consumed set committed (~128 KB total),
# multi-megabyte intermediates ignored.
#
# Day 13 adds two more (~111 KB). They are not read by the dashboard, so they sit
# outside the original rule -- but reports/paper_evidence.json cites them as the
# source of figures in the research paper, and a citation whose source is not in
# the repository cannot be checked. They are committed for that reason.
forecasts/*
!forecasts/.gitkeep
!forecasts/forward_forecasts.csv
!forecasts/interval_coverage.csv
!forecasts/holdout_evaluation.csv
!forecasts/imbalance_forecast.csv
!forecasts/early_warning_backtest.csv
!forecasts/early_warning_sensitivity.csv
!forecasts/kpi_summary.csv
!forecasts/champion_selection.csv
!forecasts/full_model_comparison.csv
!forecasts/provenance.json
!forecasts/comparison_matrix.csv
!forecasts/feature_importance.csv

# Serialized models: regenerable, and a slimmed SARIMAX result is still
# megabytes. The dashboard reads model METADATA from the registry JSON, never
# a pickle, so nothing on the deployed path needs these.
models/*.pkl
